# VitalBench data license

The VitalAgent source code is licensed separately under the MIT License in the
repository root.

To the extent that copyright or database rights apply, the VitalBench benchmark
artifacts in this directory are made available under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International license
(CC BY-NC-SA 4.0):

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

This license applies to the authors' contributions and adaptations only. It
does not replace or weaken the terms of the source datasets. Users must comply
with all applicable source-dataset licenses, attribution requirements, and
usage restrictions. In particular, commercial use is not granted for material
derived from sources licensed for non-commercial use.

No raw physiological recordings are redistributed in this repository.
VitalBench contains generated questions, answers, monitoring states, metadata,
and evaluation splits derived from the following sources:

- Icentia11k Single Lead Continuous Raw Electrocardiogram Dataset, version 1.0
  (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), https://doi.org/10.13026/kk0v-r952
- Long-term electrocardiogram and wrist-based photoplethysmogram recordings
  with annotated atrial fibrillation episodes (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0),
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11242869
- PPG-DaLiA (CC BY 4.0), https://doi.org/10.24432/C53890
- WESAD (Wearable Stress and Affect Detection),
  https://doi.org/10.24432/C57K5T; consult the linked original dataset terms

When redistributing or adapting VitalBench, retain this notice, identify any
changes, cite the applicable source datasets, and cite the VitalAgent paper as
described in the repository README.
